#Common Query
SELECT column, another_column
FROM mytable
UNION ALL/ UNION/ INTERSECTION/ EXCEPT
SELECT other_column, yet_another_column
FROM another_table
ORDER BY column DESC
LIMIT n;
*(These clause are used when you have data in different tables that can't be joined or processed)

##UNION ALL
- to append the result of one query to another assuming that they have same column count, order and data type.

##UNION
- duplicate rows between the tables will be removed from the result.

##INTERSECTION
- it ensures that only rows that are identical in both results are returned.

##EXCEPT
- it ensures that the rows from the first result that are not in the second are returned
- EXCEPT operator is query case-sensitive

*(Both except and intersection discard duplicates)
